  "notes": "Removal reference: the two removed surfaces (XSLTProcessor, XSLT PI) plus the operational contracts a developer needs to respond (timeline, deprecation trial, enterprise policy, migration paths, detection). The Chromium-vs-WHATWG IDL divergences (nullable transform returns, parameter typing, constructor raises) are documented verbatim on the xsltprocessor route. One recorded source discrepancy: pre-stable disabling is M145 in the removal guide, M148 in the ChromeStatus experiment plan. The policy-vs-trial precedence and trial token-failure behavior are unspecified in the sources and recorded as open questions in the critique."
